# Line endings are normalised to LF, and this matters here beyond tidiness.
#
# A multi-line rdfs:comment carries its line breaks inside the literal. On a
# Windows checkout those breaks are CRLF, so the Turtle and the RDF/XML of the
# same ontology ended up with different literals: git normalises the newlines
# in a .ttl file, but in RDF/XML the carriage return is escaped as a character
# entity and survives. The two serialisations then no longer agreed.
#
# Declaring the serialisations as LF text keeps them equivalent.

*.ttl  text eol=lf
*.owl  text eol=lf
*.xml  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
